n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.4$ | $0.05$ | $0.45$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.55$ | $0.45$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, using the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=2) & ={f}_{Y}(2) \\\\  & =f(1,2)+f(2,2)+f(3,2) \\\\  & =0.25+0.05+0.15 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-142562/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96760d15-5e56-529b-a5da-1697dc782031"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142562"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-142557/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" :answer/id #uuid "0a5356c5-5162-5e45-a56a-53460085ebe5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142557/selection/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26" :answer/id #uuid "dbf00ace-9c33-5b2e-98a5-6a3e61f07580" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142557/selection/0e8c61e1cbe5b6d4b3e52c0431e48b853c5faa01ca7ca0f5f9cf780292b06b1f" :answer/id #uuid "7d46262e-4406-55da-93ce-fcf75006cc0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142557/selection/9e0ecd3ac52ff99368669f5f34617bf0346b508d0e5368e317a2e814e87142d0" :answer/id #uuid "9141c099-038d-51b2-aab3-6314285529cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142557/selection/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026" :answer/id #uuid "97d79ff2-57ad-553d-ae4f-3f2c9c395f3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142557/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "802dd67f-c7f4-50a7-9efa-5ea7e2d940d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-142557/selection/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26" :answer-field/choices ["q-142557/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" "q-142557/selection/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26" "q-142557/selection/0e8c61e1cbe5b6d4b3e52c0431e48b853c5faa01ca7ca0f5f9cf780292b06b1f" "q-142557/selection/9e0ecd3ac52ff99368669f5f34617bf0346b508d0e5368e317a2e814e87142d0" "q-142557/selection/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-142557" :question/id #uuid "f0249a8c-1fbb-5835-b939-3578d912e959" :question/math-academy-id "q-142557" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ below for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ find ${f}_{Y}(2).$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.4$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.35$ | $0.25$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, using the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(2) & =f(0,2)+f(1,2) \\\\  & =0.2+0.05 \\\\  & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-142557/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96760d15-5e56-529b-a5da-1697dc782031"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142557"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-142559/selection/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" :answer/id #uuid "82b2922d-2b78-5a4e-ba18-3d059fb47d30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142559/selection/b05ae51c7e0f9ce8edef362b0e3bfd104c905bad9c2676254ee36131cb916baa" :answer/id #uuid "1a070c7d-f0cc-5b67-be85-2e2e0e166551" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142559/selection/2d5b329ffad8f2e6cddf3b1013d5c47f7be15c20228e40db178eef96670c9868" :answer/id #uuid "7ff31d70-3b48-523c-977a-4700ae71b603" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142559/selection/fafc7b5d1f3d59ecf30970324c15634804f481d2fafedc45a66f908de8bc8dd9" :answer/id #uuid "d8af2b71-db11-56b0-9d6f-becf80793ffb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142559/selection/63029caaa85c8444b7e8555b288d9c5a204814f015fb59a7e4079c09bcc12be0" :answer/id #uuid "2e6bcb1f-7037-5424-8495-568442e3dd70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142559/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7445110f-ddd2-5f85-8896-ee365bf08aef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-142559/selection/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" :answer-field/choices ["q-142559/selection/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" "q-142559/selection/b05ae51c7e0f9ce8edef362b0e3bfd104c905bad9c2676254ee36131cb916baa" "q-142559/selection/2d5b329ffad8f2e6cddf3b1013d5c47f7be15c20228e40db178eef96670c9868" "q-142559/selection/fafc7b5d1f3d59ecf30970324c15634804f481d2fafedc45a66f908de8bc8dd9" "q-142559/selection/63029caaa85c8444b7e8555b288d9c5a204814f015fb59a7e4079c09bcc12be0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-142559" :question/id #uuid "ee01b22e-38eb-5520-85b6-65e91b69b278" :question/math-academy-id "q-142559" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ below for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ find $P(Y=1).$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ |" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{9}{16}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{7}{16}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{7}{16}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, using the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=1) & ={f}_{Y}(1) \\\\  & =f(1,1)+f(2,1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-142559/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96760d15-5e56-529b-a5da-1697dc782031"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142559"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-142552/selection/57f1df4deeb63ac8b169c1392105cc1ec886c4a882da47e1d3a4a61ab32f1e2a" :answer/id #uuid "a287a941-39cf-5d42-b3ad-215fe829e3cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142552/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" :answer/id #uuid "8bac6d53-e8d5-532a-b489-fe067c6a0e3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142552/selection/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026" :answer/id #uuid "e6333532-a3fd-5b53-b5cd-7f3df872c4ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142552/selection/2468d3f08d897d95f4d28b48c13e6034ce1716985d166fd89a0b8119476fe5c8" :answer/id #uuid "302ba10f-6301-5406-a6eb-a791023086bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142552/selection/441f9a41e4c1d7c29719a73a7d795c394ee1337b1a990ebfb59a7b69a254418f" :answer/id #uuid "921de448-3d22-5cd1-a54f-e39044c7efe5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142552/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2ad0cee9-7157-5677-948e-794efe862f54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-142552/selection/441f9a41e4c1d7c29719a73a7d795c394ee1337b1a990ebfb59a7b69a254418f" :answer-field/choices ["q-142552/selection/57f1df4deeb63ac8b169c1392105cc1ec886c4a882da47e1d3a4a61ab32f1e2a" "q-142552/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" "q-142552/selection/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026" "q-142552/selection/2468d3f08d897d95f4d28b48c13e6034ce1716985d166fd89a0b8119476fe5c8" "q-142552/selection/441f9a41e4c1d7c29719a73a7d795c394ee1337b1a990ebfb59a7b69a254418f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-142552" :question/id #uuid "8031fb9a-8406-5da3-9e4c-34e027c59fc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-142552" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ below for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ find $P(Y=2).$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ |" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.4$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.5$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, using the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=2) & ={f}_{Y}(2) \\\\  & =f(1,2)+f(1,2) \\\\  & =0.4+0.3 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-142552/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96760d15-5e56-529b-a5da-1697dc782031"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142552"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-142826/selection/68dddad4aa8af344563796ca6fd03a8ad5cf4cec085d606e91dc474448e26786" :answer/id #uuid "69833fb5-a91c-5