al mass function for $Y$ is given by the following table:\n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{12}{25}$ | $\\frac{13}{25}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-142834/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac80eed8-d801-5275-9bd1-73ba43fadb38"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142834"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-142572/selection/e459c513a8ab41d90fbedd18ffc02e71387b30263f9b62ed7d74cc4e1864eeb6" :answer/id #uuid "ae15abf1-e86a-5111-b4c9-da11bd1a9069" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.55" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142572/selection/441f9a41e4c1d7c29719a73a7d795c394ee1337b1a990ebfb59a7b69a254418f" :answer/id #uuid "276c5ae6-df9d-5f8e-9807-2e0d616e5f11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142572/selection/bc99aa5f3ee62c40cb834b274ce88683dbffd8fee8404db2b536df0189aa9cdc" :answer/id #uuid "561f4d55-6954-53f7-b0ec-98d22fb329c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142572/selection/a44ed9268297050614edc4097a04d3089044bc70b376ad604b0445193a602b0a" :answer/id #uuid "48deacc9-2775-5153-beaa-0f9bfc574a4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.65" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142572/selection/57f27b4de16f64fcab2f3b810a7087fb3b270a063a6807c410b738013ce41fde" :answer/id #uuid "d8deb50e-79b6-56a9-ac5d-47c4501b81ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142572/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4b06fa8-953d-5e68-94fe-9d9930d8ac21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-142572/selection/57f27b4de16f64fcab2f3b810a7087fb3b270a063a6807c410b738013ce41fde" :answer-field/choices ["q-142572/selection/e459c513a8ab41d90fbedd18ffc02e71387b30263f9b62ed7d74cc4e1864eeb6" "q-142572/selection/441f9a41e4c1d7c29719a73a7d795c394ee1337b1a990ebfb59a7b69a254418f" "q-142572/selection/bc99aa5f3ee62c40cb834b274ce88683dbffd8fee8404db2b536df0189aa9cdc" "q-142572/selection/a44ed9268297050614edc4097a04d3089044bc70b376ad604b0445193a602b0a" "q-142572/selection/57f27b4de16f64fcab2f3b810a7087fb3b270a063a6807c410b738013ce41fde"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-142572" :question/id #uuid "8fa0761f-0e18-5863-ae2f-db25cb746dc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-142572" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.35$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ |\n\nGiven the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ above for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ calculate $P(X<2).$" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.35$ | $0.1$ | $0.45$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.55$ | $0.45$ | $1$ |\n\nThe marginal mass function for $X$ is given in the following table:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.35$ | $0.45$ | $0.2$ |\n\nFinally, using the table of values of the marginal mass function for $X,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<2) & =P(X\\in {0,1}) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=1) \\\\  & =0.35+0.45 \\\\  & =0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-142572/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96473ec4-67f8-5614-b187-0961062aac29"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142572"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-142718/selection/0e8c61e1cbe5b6d4b3e52c0431e48b853c5faa01ca7ca0f5f9cf780292b06b1f" :answer/id #uuid "e7d571aa-54e3-5759-ace3-f24cd16bc673" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142718/selection/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026" :answer/id #uuid "97aecea0-a36d-54e2-8eee-0e837887b041" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142718/selection/a44ed9268297050614edc4097a04d3089044bc70b376ad604b0445193a602b0a" :answer/id #uuid "fb7efe77-b797-5937-bd53-c7290168dca6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.65" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142718/selection/bd0c5293c05dbcd56341c67931e9e0ae46e20e1d0de3da140e1b2dcd87ea42e2" :answer/id #uuid "79f25296-1781-5f7f-9f15-87fab5e1f98e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142718/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" :answer/id #uuid "baf84851-495f-5c91-bc72-1eea31f3c289" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142718/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "12d342d1-92cb-5e54-b57b-4ba693b2bea6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-142718/selection/a44ed9268297050614edc4097a04d3089044bc70b376ad604b0445193a602b0a" :answer-field/choices ["q-142718/selection/0e8c61e1cbe5b6d4b3e52c0431e48b853c5faa01ca7ca0f5f9cf780292b06b1f" "q-142718/selection/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026" "q-142718/selection/a44ed9268297050614edc4097a04d3089044bc70b376ad604b0445193a602b0a" "q-142718/selection/bd0c5293c05dbcd56341c67931e9e0ae46e20e1d0de3da140e1b2dcd87ea42e2" "q-142718/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-142718" :question/id #uuid "9c560696-9fe2-5c0b-8c1e-d2fdd8325ece" :question/math-academy-id "q-142718" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=-1$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ |\n\nGiven the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ above for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ calculate $P(|Y|>0).$" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=-1$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $0.55$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ | $0.45$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.2$ | $0.35$ | $0.45$ | $1$ |\n\nThe marginal mass function for $Y$ is given in the following table:\n\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.2$ | $0.35$ | $0.45$ |\n\nFinally, using the table of values of the marginal mass function for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(|Y|>0) & =P(Y\\in {-1,1}) \\\\  & =P(Y=-1)+P(Y=1) \\\\  & =0.2+0.45 \\\\  & =0.65.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-142718/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96473ec4-67f8-5614-b187-0961062aac29"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142718"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-po