a350-14b4fab5ebd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-142723" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |\n\nGiven the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ above for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ calculate $P(Y\\ge 1).$" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.5$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.55$ | $0.2$ | $0.25$ | $1$ |\n\nThe marginal mass function for $Y$ is given in the following table:\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.55$ | $0.2$ | $0.25$ |\n\nFinally, using the table of values of the marginal mass function for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\ge 1) & =P(Y\\in {1,2}) \\\\  & =P(Y=1)+P(Y=2) \\\\  & =0.2+0.25 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-142723/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96473ec4-67f8-5614-b187-0961062aac29"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142723"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-142575/selection/4582dbd6025ba0c110f8e23964efc62e8612751348ffad003e8834a5780c1878" :answer/id #uuid "b0e57118-95ef-5cf1-abe2-d2aa68db8b32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\